config MB_LAB_PROCTHREAD
	tristate "concurrency lab: char device hammered by threads + processes"
	default m
	help
	  A misc device /dev/mb_procthread whose write() bumps a mutex-protected
	  counter. The user_procthread tool drives it from pthreads and fork()'d
	  processes at once; the counter stays exact, and each open() logs
	  pid/tgid so you see the kernel's thread-vs-process view.
